      "id": 1,
      "text": "Casco was incorporated as a town on March 18, 1841, after separating from Raymond.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casco%2C_Maine",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The area began as Raymondtown Plantation, granted in 1767 to Captain William Raymond of Beverly.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Casco_Maine",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Water-powered mills sprang up after separation, including four sawmills, four gristmills, a shook mill, and a tannery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Casco_Maine",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Crooked River, the longest tributary to Sebago Lake, supplies 38% of the lake’s inflow and vital salmon habitat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Casco_Maine",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The historic Songo Locks on the Songo River let hand‑operated gates move boats between Sebago Lake and upstream lakes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Casco_Maine",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Casco hosts Casco Days, an annual fair held each July’s last Saturday in Casco Days Park.",
